  "summary": "Live dev-session findings: (1) stage-task creation made an explicit, unconditional flow step in both dev and design routers instead of disconnected descriptive prose that got skipped entirely in one run; (2) Implement Step 3's developer sign-off ask adapted to what a step actually became instead of a rigid restatement of the plan's verification text, plus removal of reflexive duplicate check execution between a delegated worker and the orchestrator; (3) anti-fabrication hardening banning `check record --source developer` (or marking a step Done/complete) without an actual developer reply in the conversation, after a live incident where self-run checks were falsely attributed to the developer with invented evidence text.",
